{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GovXX3k9WU4DzjupajcXsN","type":"tool_result","content":"default:\n    @just --list\n\nbuild:\n    sbt compile\n\ntest:\n    sbt test\n\nfmt:\n    sbt scalafmtAll\n\n# point git at the versioned hooks so `just check` runs before every commit\ninstall-hooks:\n    git config core.hooksPath .githooks\n    chmod +x .githooks/pre-commit\n\n# scalafmt, compile with -Werror, tests\n@check:\n    #!/usr/bin/env bash\n    set -euo pipefail\n    log=$(mktemp)\n    trap 'rm -f \"$log\"' EXIT\n    sbt -batch scalafmtCheckAll test | tee \"$log\"\n    echo\n    scala_files=$(find src -name '*.scala')\n    lines=0\n    [ -z \"$scala_files\" ] || lines=$(cat $scala_files | grep -c .)\n    echo \"scala   : $lines lines in $(echo \"$scala_files\" | grep -c . || true) files\"\n    grep '^\\[info\\] Passed: ' \"$log\" | sed 's/^\\[info\\] Passed: /tests   : /' || echo \"tests   : 0\"\n    echo \"warnings: $(grep -c '^\\[warn\\]' \"$log\" || true)\"\n\n# Deterministic spec structure gate (Scala checker; v13.M12).\nspec-check:\n    ./scripts/spec-check-scala/run docs/specs\n\n# Copy/paste redundancy gate (outer.v15.M4). Accepts verbosity=quiet|normal|verbose,\n# report=PATH, and any tool flag, e.g. `just check-redundancies --fail-on-findings`.\n# The tool is PMD CPD (pinned in scripts/check-redundancies-cpd/build.sbt); silence a region with `// CPD-OFF` ... `// CPD-ON`.\n[positional-arguments]\ncheck-redundancies *args:\n    #!/usr/bin/env bash\n    set -euo pipefail\n    verbosity=quiet\n    report=snapshots/redundancy-report.json\n    rest=()\n    for a in \"$@\"; do\n      case \"$a\" in\n        verbosity=*) verbosity=\"${a#verbosity=}\" ;;\n        report=*) report=\"${a#report=}\" ;;\n        *) rest+=(\"$a\") ;;\n      esac\n    done\n    exec ./scripts/check-redundancies src --verbosity \"$verbosity\" --report \"$report\" ${rest[@]+\"${rest[@]}\"}\n---SKILL---\n===.claude/skills/check-redundancies/SKILL.md===\n---\nname: check-redundancies\ndescription: Run the copy/paste redundancy gate (PMD CPD) and surface top findings ordered by size times occurrences. Use when asked about redundancy, copy-paste, CPD, or duplicated Scala blocks.\n---\n\n# /check-redundancies\n\nThe gate is PMD's copy/paste detector (CPD, pinned in `scripts/check-redundancies-cpd/build.sbt`) run through the JDK and sbt. The first run builds it and fetches the pinned PMD jars once; later runs are offline.\n\n1. Run `just check-redundancies` (default verbosity `quiet`, minimum 50 tokens) from the app/lesson root.\n2. Read the JSON report (`snapshots/redundancy-report.json` by default): `finding_count`, then the findings.\n3. Present findings ordered by **impact = lines × occurrences** (the tool already sorts this way). Show file:start for each location.\n4. For each top finding, propose one concrete refactor: parameterize a function, introduce an abstraction, push code up/down the call hierarchy, or localize responsibility in the domain model.\n5. Re-run after fixes with `just check-redundancies --fail-on-findings`; it exits non-zero while findings remain. Use `verbosity=verbose` to see the duplicated snippet.\n6. Removing the duplication is the goal. Only when a duplicate is intentional, silence exactly that region with `// CPD-OFF` ... `// CPD-ON` around it, or exclude a path with `--allow '**/generated/**'`, and say why (M4d).\n---SRC TREE---\nsrc/main/resources/reference.conf\nsrc/main/scala/.gitkeep\nsrc/main/scala/todo/Cli.scala\nsrc/main/scala/todo/Greeting.scala\nsrc/main/scala/todo/Main.scala\nsrc/main/scala/todo/config/AppConfig.scala\nsrc/main/scala/todo/core/Title.scala\nsrc/main/scala/todo/core/Todo.scala\nsrc/main/scala/todo/core/TodoId.scala\nsrc/main/scala/todo/core/Todos.scala\nsrc/main/scala/todo/render/Renderer.scala\nsrc/main/scala/todo/store/Store.scala\nsrc/main/scala/todo/store/TodoRecord.scala\nsrc/test/scala/.gitkeep\nsrc/test/scala/todo/CliSuite.scala\nsrc/test/scala/todo/GreetingSuite.scala\nsrc/test/scala/todo/config/AppConfigSuite.scala\nsrc/test/scala/todo/core/TitleSuite.scala\nsrc/test/scala/todo/core/TodosPropertySuite.scala\nsrc/test/scala/todo/core/TodosSuite.scala\nsrc/test/scala/todo/render/RendererSuite.scala\nsrc/test/scala/todo/store/StoreSuite.scala","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0fc5fc0f-850e-4402-a968-b5ac1a7c33e5","uuid":"aee27eef-8fdc-4d10-809a-264a191db7ca","timestamp":"2026-09-30T07:12:18.739Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"default:\n    @just --list\n\nbuild:\n    sbt compile\n\ntest:\n    sbt test\n\nfmt:\n    sbt scalafmtAll\n\n# point git at the versioned hooks so `just check` runs before every commit\ninstall-hooks:\n    git config core.hooksPath .githooks\n    chmod +x .githooks/pre-commit\n\n# scalafmt, compile with -Werror, tests\n@check:\n    #!/usr/bin/env bash\n    set -euo pipefail\n    log=$(mktemp)\n    trap 'rm -f \"$log\"' EXIT\n    sbt -batch scalafmtCheckAll test | tee \"$log\"\n    echo\n    scala_files=$(find src -name '*.scala')\n    lines=0\n    [ -z \"$scala_files\" ] || lines=$(cat $scala_files | grep -c .)\n    echo \"scala   : $lines lines in $(echo \"$scala_files\" | grep -c . || true) files\"\n    grep '^\\[info\\] Passed: ' \"$log\" | sed 's/^\\[info\\] Passed: /tests   : /' || echo \"tests   : 0\"\n    echo \"warnings: $(grep -c '^\\[warn\\]' \"$log\" || true)\"\n\n# Deterministic spec structure gate (Scala checker; v13.M12).\nspec-check:\n    ./scripts/spec-check-scala/run docs/specs\n\n# Copy/paste redundancy gate (outer.v15.M4). Accepts verbosity=quiet|normal|verbose,\n# report=PATH, and any tool flag, e.g. `just check-redundancies --fail-on-findings`.\n# The tool is PMD CPD (pinned in scripts/check-redundancies-cpd/build.sbt); silence a region with `// CPD-OFF` ... `// CPD-ON`.\n[positional-arguments]\ncheck-redundancies *args:\n    #!/usr/bin/env bash\n    set -euo pipefail\n    verbosity=quiet\n    report=snapshots/redundancy-report.json\n    rest=()\n